# Appendix B. Minimum information to preserve across conversations/models

A fresh model receiving only this plan and the repository should be able to continue if it preserves these facts:

- at run bootstrap, fresh-fetch `plan/remediation`, pin the exact Plan SHA, and read the complete canonical plan by concatenating `remediation/master-plan/parts/*.part` in lexical order;
- do not silently switch Plan SHA mid-run; implementation/review/ledger remain live-fetched, while the Plan SHA is the pinned governance snapshot unless the user explicitly changes it;
- always fresh-fetch implementation, `review/remediation`, and ledger branches during remediation/review cycles;
- current SHAs written in this document are anchors, never assumed latest;
- Finding A is independently CLEAN and ledger-closed unless fresh regression evidence exists;
- BUG-OUTPUT-01 is the current first gate at plan generation;
- Finding B is gated behind BUG-OUTPUT-01 independent CLEAN, but unrelated actionable defects may proceed asynchronously while review is pending;
- after Finding B independent CLEAN, full current-source F1 / BUG-BACKUP-01 close-out is mandatory before downstream backup/restore work relies on F1 closure;
- implementation history is additive only;
- self-review never equals independent CLEAN;
- an ancestor SHA's independent CLEAN may unlock a dependency on a later current HEAD only after Section 11.5.1's intervening-commit carry-forward guard succeeds; shared-domain changes require current-candidate regression evidence and, when semantic preservation is uncertain, a new independent review;
- `review/remediation` is the official additive independent-review history and targets exact implementation SHAs;
- a later review-fix for an older defect is added on current HEAD rather than rebasing history;
- no pending review, dependency, evidence gap, product decision, device, or unchanged review branch may idle the runner while unrelated actionable work exists; before stopping for lack of work, exhaustively rescan the full registry and open review-fixes under Section 11.2.1;
- `NO_CHANGE_REQUIRED_CURRENT_HEAD` and `NOT_APPLICABLE_CURRENT_HEAD` permit the runner to move on but never substitute for independent CLEAN;
- ledger closure records only already-established independent decisions;
- legacy F3–F22 invariants remain available even when the current priority queue differs;
- current source beats planning hypotheses;
- evidence vocabulary must remain exact;
- Samsung unavailable wording is `NOT EXECUTED — DEVICE UNAVAILABLE`;
- after correctness remediation, token auto-extractor is separate feature work.

